# Thuli Billings — Core

- Prioritize an **extremely fast**, user-friendly UI (especially POS billing).
- Keep architecture **simple** and **modular**. Do not over-engineer.
- Prefer feature folders over deep abstraction layers, shared “core frameworks”, or premature packages.
- Keep the database **light** (SQLite local + Supabase remote). Avoid extra tables, warehouses, or sync complexity unless required.
- Payments: Razorpay on the website only; the app only checks paid / subscription status.
- Follow [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md). Do not invent data models until the user provides them.
- Stage order: scaffold → models → UI → sync → analytics/invoices → website.
- Website: never add decorative gradient bubbles / radial tint blobs in backgrounds (see AGENTS.md).
